# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `problem` and `problem_type` arguments encode an optimization problem of"
" the form\n"
msgstr ""
"Les arguments `problem` et `problem_type` encodent un problème "
"d'optimisation de la forme\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\n"
"\\min_{(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\in D} C(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\nonumber\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
"where\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align}\n"
"\\min_{(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\in D} C(x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n) \\nonumber\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
"où\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C(x_1, ... , x_n) = a + \\sum_{i} b_i x_i + \\sum_{i, j} c_{i, j} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum_{k_1, ..., k_m} g_{k_1, ..., k_m} x_{k_1} ... x_{k_m}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C(x_1, ... , x_n) = a + \\sum_{i} b_i x_i + \\sum_{i, j} c_{i, j} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum_{k_1, ..., k_m} g_{k_1, ..., k_m} x_{k_1} ... x_{k_m}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By choosing `problem_type = \"binary\"`, you specify that the cost function "
"is in `binary` format, which means that $D = \\{0,  1\\}^{n}$, as in, the "
"cost function is written in QUBO/HUBO formulation.\n"
msgstr ""
"En choisissant `problem_type = \"binary\"`, tu spécifies que la fonction de "
"coût est au format `binary`, ce qui signifie que $D = \\{0,  1\\}^{n}$, "
"c'est-à-dire que la fonction de coût est écrite sous forme QUBO/HUBO.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the other hand, by choosing `problem_type = \"spin\"`, the cost function "
"is written in Ising formulation, where $D = \\{-1, 1\\}^{n}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"D'autre part, en choisissant `problem_type = \"spin\"`, la fonction de coût "
"est écrite sous forme Ising, où $D = \\{-1, 1\\}^{n}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The coefficients of the problem should be encoded in a dictionary as follows:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align} \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\{} \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"()\"}&: \\quad &a, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i,)\"}&: \\quad &b_i, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i, j)\"}&: \\quad &c_{i, j}, \\quad (i \\neq j) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\quad  \\vdots \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(} k_1, ..., k_m  \\texttt{)\"}&: \\quad &g_{k_1, ..., k_m}, \\quad (k_1 \\neq k_2 \\neq \\dots \\neq k_m) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\}}\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Les coefficients du problème doivent être encodés dans un dictionnaire comme suit :\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align} \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\{} \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"()\"}&: \\quad &a, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i,)\"}&: \\quad &b_i, \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(i, j)\"}&: \\quad &c_{i, j}, \\quad (i \\neq j) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\quad  \\vdots \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\"(} k_1, ..., k_m  \\texttt{)\"}&: \\quad &g_{k_1, ..., k_m}, \\quad (k_1 \\neq k_2 \\neq \\dots \\neq k_m) \\\\ \\nonumber\n"
"&\\texttt{\\}}\n"
"\\end{align}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that the keys of the dictionary must be strings containing a valid "
"tuple of non-repeating integers. For binary problems, we know that:\n"
msgstr ""
"Note que les clés du dictionnaire doivent être des chaînes de caractères "
"contenant un tuple valide d'entiers non répétés. Pour les problèmes "
"binaires, nous savons que :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"x_i^2 = x_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"x_i^2 = x_i\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for $i=j$ (since $x_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$ means $x_i \\cdot x_i = x_i$). So, in "
"your QUBO formulation, if you have both linear contributions $b_i x_i$ and "
"diagonal quadratic contributions $c_{i,i} x_i^2$, these terms must be "
"combined into a single linear coefficient:\n"
msgstr ""
"pour $i=j$ (puisque $x_i \\in \\{0,1\\}$ implique $x_i \\cdot x_i = x_i$). "
"Ainsi, dans ta formulation QUBO, si tu as à la fois des contributions "
"linéaires $b_i x_i$ et des contributions quadratiques diagonales $c_{i,i} "
"x_i^2$, ces termes doivent être combinés en un seul coefficient linéaire :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Total linear coefficient for variable $x_i$:** $b_i + c_{i,i}$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Coefficient linéaire total pour la variable $x_i$ :** $b_i + c_{i,i}$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This means:\n"
"- Linear terms like `\"(i, )\"` contain: original linear coefficient + diagonal quadratic coefficient\n"
"- Diagonal quadratic terms like `\"(i, i)\"` should **NOT** appear in the final dictionary\n"
"- Only off-diagonal quadratic terms like `\"(i, j)\"` where $i \\neq j$ should be included as separate entries\n"
msgstr ""
"Cela signifie :\n"
"- Les termes linéaires comme `\"(i, )\"` contiennent : le coefficient linéaire original + le coefficient quadratique diagonal\n"
"- Les termes quadratiques diagonaux comme `\"(i, i)\"` ne doivent **PAS** apparaître dans le dictionnaire final\n"
"- Seuls les termes quadratiques hors diagonale comme `\"(i, j)\"` où $i \\neq j$ doivent être inclus comme entrées séparées\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Example:** If your QUBO has $3x_1 + 2x_1^2 + 4x_1 x_2$, the Iskay dictionary should contain:\n"
"- `\"(0, )\"`: `5.0` (combining $3 + 2 = 5$)\n"
"- `\"(0, 1)\"`: `4.0` (off-diagonal term)\n"
msgstr ""
"**Exemple :** Si ton QUBO contient $3x_1 + 2x_1^2 + 4x_1 x_2$, le dictionnaire Iskay doit contenir :\n"
"- `\"(0, )\"` : `5.0` (combinaison de $3 + 2 = 5$)\n"
"- `\"(0, 1)\"` : `4.0` (terme hors diagonale)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**NOT** separate entries for `\"(0, )\"`: `3.0` and `\"(0, 0)\"`: `2.0`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Et **NON** des entrées séparées pour `\"(0, )\"` : `3.0` et `\"(0, 0)\"` : "
"`2.0`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Understand the bf-DCQO algorithm {#understand-the-bf-dcqo-algorithm}"
msgstr "Comprendre l'algorithme bf-DCQO {#understand-the-bf-dcqo-algorithm}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we run the optimization, let's understand the sophisticated quantum "
"algorithm that powers Iskay: **bf-DCQO (bias-field digitized counterdiabatic"
" quantum optimization)** [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Avant de lancer l'optimisation, comprenons l'algorithme quantique "
"sophistiqué qui alimente Iskay : **bf-DCQO (bias-field digitized "
"counterdiabatic quantum optimization)** [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What is bf-DCQO? {#what-is-bf-dcqo}"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que bf-DCQO ? {#what-is-bf-dcqo}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"bf-DCQO is based on the time evolution of a quantum system where the problem"
" solution is encoded in the **ground state** (lowest energy state) of the "
"final quantum Hamiltonian [\\[1\\]](#references). The algorithm addresses a "
"fundamental challenge in quantum optimization:\n"
msgstr ""
"bf-DCQO est basé sur l'évolution temporelle d'un système quantique où la "
"solution du problème est encodée dans l'**état fondamental** (état d'énergie"
" le plus bas) du Hamiltonien quantique final [\\[1\\]](#references). "
"L'algorithme répond à un défi fondamental de l'optimisation quantique :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The challenge**: Traditional adiabatic quantum computing requires very "
"slow evolution to maintain ground state conditions according to the "
"adiabatic theorem. This demands increasingly deep quantum circuits as "
"problem complexity grows, leading to more gate operations and accumulated "
"errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Le défi** : le calcul quantique adiabatique traditionnel nécessite une "
"évolution très lente pour maintenir les conditions de l'état fondamental "
"conformément au théorème adiabatique. Cela exige des circuits quantiques de "
"plus en plus profonds à mesure que la complexité du problème augmente, "
"entraînant davantage d'opérations de portes et d'erreurs accumulées.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The solution**: bf-DCQO uses counterdiabatic protocols to enable rapid "
"evolution while maintaining ground state fidelity, dramatically reducing "
"circuit depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"**La solution** : bf-DCQO utilise des protocoles contreadiabatiques pour "
"permettre une évolution rapide tout en maintenant la fidélité de l'état "
"fondamental, réduisant considérablement la profondeur des circuits.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical framework {#mathematical-framework}"
msgstr "Cadre mathématique {#mathematical-framework}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The algorithm minimizes a cost function of the form:\n"
msgstr "L'algorithme minimise une fonction de coût de la forme :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\min_{(x_1,x_2,...,x_n) \\in D} C(x_1,x_2,...,x_n)$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\min_{(x_1,x_2,...,x_n) \\in D} C(x_1,x_2,...,x_n)$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "where $D = \\{0,1\\}^n$ for binary variables and:\n"
msgstr "où $D = \\{0,1\\}^n$ pour les variables binaires et :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$C(x) = a + \\sum_i b_i x_i + \\sum_{i,j} c_{ij} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum "
"g_{k_1,...,k_m} x_{k_1}...x_{k_m}$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$C(x) = a + \\sum_i b_i x_i + \\sum_{i,j} c_{ij} x_i x_j + ... + \\sum "
"g_{k_1,...,k_m} x_{k_1}...x_{k_m}$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For our Market Split problem, the cost function is:\n"
msgstr "Pour notre problème de Market Split, la fonction de coût est :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$C(x) = ||Ax - b||^2 = x^T A^T A x - 2 b^T A x + b^T b$$\n"
msgstr "$$C(x) = ||Ax - b||^2 = x^T A^T A x - 2 b^T A x + b^T b$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The role of counterdiabatic terms {#the-role-of-counterdiabatic-terms}"
msgstr ""
"Le rôle des termes contreadiabatiques {#the-role-of-counterdiabatic-terms}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Counterdiabatic terms** are additional terms introduced into the time-"
"dependent Hamiltonian that suppress unwanted excitations during the quantum "
"evolution. Here's why they're crucial:\n"
msgstr ""
"Les **termes contreadiabatiques** sont des termes supplémentaires introduits"
" dans le Hamiltonien dépendant du temps qui suppriment les excitations "
"indésirables pendant l'évolution quantique. Voici pourquoi ils sont "
"essentiels :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In adiabatic quantum optimization, we evolve the system according to a time-"
"dependent Hamiltonian:\n"
msgstr ""
"En optimisation quantique adiabatique, nous faisons évoluer le système selon"
" un Hamiltonien dépendant du temps :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$H(t) = \\left(1 - \\frac{t}{T}\\right) H_{\\text{initial}} + \\frac{t}{T} "
"H_{\\text{problem}}$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$H(t) = \\left(1 - \\frac{t}{T}\\right) H_{\\text{initial}} + \\frac{t}{T} "
"H_{\\text{problem}}$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $H_{\\text{problem}}$ encodes our optimization problem. To maintain "
"the ground state during rapid evolution, we add counterdiabatic terms:\n"
msgstr ""
"où $H_{\\text{problem}}$ encode notre problème d'optimisation. Pour "
"maintenir l'état fondamental lors d'une évolution rapide, nous ajoutons des "
"termes contreadiabatiques :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$H_{\\text{CD}}(t) = H(t) + H_{\\text{counter}}(t)$$\n"
msgstr "$$H_{\\text{CD}}(t) = H(t) + H_{\\text{counter}}(t)$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These counterdiabatic terms do the following:\n"
"1. **Suppress unwanted transitions**: Prevent the quantum state from jumping to excited states during fast evolution\n"
"2. **Enable shorter evolution times**: Allow us to reach the final state much faster without violating adiabaticity\n"
"3. **Reduce circuit depth**: Shorter evolution leads to fewer gates and less error\n"
msgstr ""
"Ces termes contreadiabatiques ont les effets suivants :\n"
"1. **Suppression des transitions indésirables** : empêchent l'état quantique de sauter vers des états excités lors d'une évolution rapide\n"
"2. **Temps d'évolution plus courts** : permettent d'atteindre l'état final beaucoup plus rapidement sans violer l'adiabaticité\n"
"3. **Réduction de la profondeur des circuits** : une évolution plus courte conduit à moins de portes et moins d'erreurs\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The practical impact is dramatic: bf-DCQO uses up to **10 times fewer "
"entangling gates** than Digital Quantum Annealing [\\[1\\]](#references), "
"making it practical for today's noisy quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"L'impact pratique est spectaculaire : bf-DCQO utilise jusqu'à **10 fois "
"moins de portes intriquantes** que le Digital Quantum Annealing "
"[\\[1\\]](#references), le rendant praticable sur le matériel quantique "
"bruyant d'aujourd'hui.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bias-field iterative optimization {#bias-field-iterative-optimization}"
msgstr ""
"Optimisation itérative par champ de biais {#bias-field-iterative-"
"optimization}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unlike variational algorithms that optimize circuit parameters through many "
"iterations, bf-DCQO uses a **bias-field guided approach** that converges in "
"approximately 10 iterations [1]:\n"
msgstr ""
"Contrairement aux algorithmes variationnels qui optimisent les paramètres du"
" circuit à travers de nombreuses itérations, bf-DCQO utilise une **approche "
"guidée par champ de biais** qui converge en environ 10 itérations [1] :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Iteration process:**\n"
msgstr "**Processus itératif :**\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Initial quantum evolution**: Start with a quantum circuit implementing the"
" counterdiabatic evolution protocol\n"
msgstr ""
"**Évolution quantique initiale** : démarrer avec un circuit quantique "
"implémentant le protocole d'évolution contreadiabatique\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Measurement**: Measure the quantum state to obtain a probability "
"distribution over bitstrings\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mesure** : mesurer l'état quantique pour obtenir une distribution de "
"probabilité sur les chaînes de bits\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Bias-field calculation**: Analyze the measurement statistics and calculate an optimal bias-field $h_i$ for each qubit:\n"
"$$h_i = \\text{f}(\\text{measurement statistics}, \\text{previous solutions})$$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Calcul du champ de biais** : analyser les statistiques de mesure et calculer un champ de biais optimal $h_i$ pour chaque qubit :\n"
"$$h_i = \\text{f}(\\text{measurement statistics}, \\text{previous solutions})$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Next iteration**: The bias-field modifies the Hamiltonian for the next iteration:\n"
"$$H_{\\text{next}} = H_{\\text{problem}} + \\sum_i h_i \\sigma_i^z$$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Itération suivante** : le champ de biais modifie le Hamiltonien pour l'itération suivante :\n"
"$$H_{\\text{next}} = H_{\\text{problem}} + \\sum_i h_i \\sigma_i^z$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   This allows starting near the previously found good solution, effectively"
" performing a form of \"quantum local search\"\n"
msgstr ""
"   Cela permet de démarrer près de la bonne solution trouvée précédemment, "
"effectuant ainsi une forme de « recherche locale quantique »\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Convergence**: Repeat until the solution quality stabilizes or a maximum "
"number of iterations is reached\n"
msgstr ""
"**Convergence** : répéter jusqu'à ce que la qualité de la solution se "
"stabilise ou qu'un nombre maximal d'itérations soit atteint\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Key advantage**: Each iteration provides meaningful progress toward the "
"optimal solution by incorporating information from previous measurements, "
"unlike variational methods that must explore the parameter space blindly.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Avantage clé** : chaque itération apporte une progression significative "
"vers la solution optimale en incorporant les informations des mesures "
"précédentes, contrairement aux méthodes variationnelles qui doivent explorer"
" l'espace des paramètres à l'aveugle.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Integrated classical post-processing {#integrated-classical-post-processing}"
msgstr ""
"Post-traitement classique intégré {#integrated-classical-post-processing}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After the quantum optimization converges, Iskay performs classical **local "
"search** post-processing:\n"
msgstr ""
"Après la convergence de l'optimisation quantique, Iskay effectue un post-"
"traitement classique de **recherche locale** :\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Bit-flip exploration**: Systematically or randomly flip bits in the best "
"measured solution\n"
msgstr ""
"**Exploration par inversion de bits** : inverser systématiquement ou "
"aléatoirement des bits dans la meilleure solution mesurée\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Energy evaluation**: Calculate $C(x)$ for each modified solution\n"
msgstr ""
"**Évaluation de l'énergie** : calculer $C(x)$ pour chaque solution "
"modifiée\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Greedy selection**: Accept improvements that lower the cost function\n"
msgstr ""
"**Sélection gloutonne** : accepter les améliorations qui diminuent la "
"fonction de coût\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Multiple passes**: Perform several passes (controlled by "
"`postprocessing_level`)\n"
msgstr ""
"**Passes multiples** : effectuer plusieurs passes (contrôlées par "
"`postprocessing_level`)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This hybrid approach compensates for bit-flip errors from hardware "
"imperfections and readout errors, ensuring high-quality solutions even on "
"noisy quantum devices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cette approche hybride compense les erreurs d'inversion de bits dues aux "
"imperfections matérielles et aux erreurs de lecture, garantissant des "
"solutions de haute qualité même sur des dispositifs quantiques bruyants.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
